    "findings": {
      "type7_low20": "Exact separate native branch sets parent RTBuddy IOPstatus8 Running, with no prior7 check. It never sets Sleep2 and cannot qualify a PWRGATE ACK.",
      "shutdown_ack": "Native type7 low1/2 requires prior host IOPstatus7 and sets2; low0 requires7 and sets1. Frozen limited shutdown predicate remains low1/2 only.",
      "validate_correction": "Default _iopValidate expects8 when parent host bytes100/108 bit0 are both clear; either bit set expects6 Ready. Earlier blanket normal-route6 wording is overbroad and is corrected here, without rewriting frozen evidence.",
      "host_on": "Native _signalApPowerGated(ON1) maps20, sends EP0 typeB20 if management remote-state field108 is not20, waits for20 and checks it. TypeB dispatch stores low32 into that remote field and wakes. This is separate from parent hostflag108.",
      "order": "Outer changePowerState calls routes before perform(new,old), then routes after perform(current,current); management ON1/oldON1 callback signals APON20 subject to skip flag123/remote-state match. Native performON validates host IOPstate before completion. Conservative ordered experiment waits boot7/20, sends one B20, waits fresh exact B20, then202.",
      "applicability": "Saved nub compatible rtbuddy-v2 matches generic RTBuddy, not ARG; saved relevant nodes lack both properties. This supports generic default8. Live native runtime object flags, skip123 and previously observed remote-state value are unbound; always issuing oneB20 is a conservative observed-protocol hypothesis, not full native parity.",
      "actual_gap": "Second START readback CTRL10 and HELLO12+two exact map ACKs succeeded. Own202 write path then ran before boot20 observation; fourth frame is boot7/20, rejected before stop/OFF/put. Causality between that frame and202 is not proved. Cold startup independently receives the same7/20 then sendsB20/waitsB20 before joined context; no INIT220.",
      "retention": "Current second reference retained1/ACTIVE. Host identities174 remain pinned. Objects/owned contents change across first/cycle/later; cycle-owned and later-owned match, original receive journal51176 is unchanged, but none proves global GPU cessation or DMA retirement."
    },
